WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.340
<b>Vivi's Adventure</b>

3
00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.540
We've got trouble!

4
00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:06.490
Vivi! Where are they?

5
00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.520
Oh, Igaram, what is it?

6
00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.020
Luffy and all the others.

7
00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.090
Where are they?

8
00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.700
The sea. They are pirates.

9
00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:18.000
Oh, no.

10
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:22.490
Listen up, you guys.
Pirates are nothing but scum.

11
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.120
<b>"Turncoat" Jango
Private Third Class
Marine Headquarters</b>

12
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.520
Every one of them.

13
00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:25.420
Hey, wait.
Don't you remember?

14
00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:29.090
<b>"Ironfist" Fullbody
Private Third Class
Marine Headquarters</b>

15
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.590
What are you saying?

16
00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:29.400
Come on. You used to be one.

17
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.400
You're right!
How could I forget?

18
00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:33.470
Uh-huh, oh, baby!

19
00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.900
Let's dance!

20
00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.780
Aw, yeah! Dance! Dance!

21
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.630
That's right, in a funky style!

22
00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:47.360
<b>Nanohana Port
Kingdom of Arabasta</b>

23
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.060
It looks like those
two subdued the enemy ship.

24
00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:46.660
It took them long enough.

25
00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.000
Don't tell me.
They're dancing, right?

26
00:02:49.050 --> 00:02:51.010
I trusted those two to
finish off that pirate ship

27
00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.480
that tried to escape us
and this is what they do.

28
00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:56.040
Disappointed.
Hina's disappointed.

29
00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.810
Have you finished deploying all the ships?

30
00:02:57.880 --> 00:02:59.080
Yes, that's affirmative, Ma'am!

31
00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.040
Every harbor in this
dust ball of a country

32
00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.380
is now blockaded!

33
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:04.490
But, Ma'am.

34
00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:05.360
Hm?

35
00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.920
There's one thing I'm concerned about.

36
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:07.850
What's that?

37
00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.260
Well, it's just the
Straw Hats' ship, ma'am.

38
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.600
It was confirmed to be
near Erumalu, and now...

39
00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.640
...it's gone.

40
00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.660
Don't tell me they've
left the country already!

41
00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:17.020
No! I doubt that, Ma'am!

42
00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.790
Then go search for it!
Scour the entire coast!

43
00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.570
Yes! Right away!

44
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:22.700
Oh, no.

45
00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.910
Miss Hina!
We're sorry it took us so long.

46
00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:27.410
Aren't you gonna
ask us why it took so long?

47
00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.610
Why'd it take so long?

48
00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.420
Because we were picking these
flowers for you, Miss Hina!

49
00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:33.790
No thanks. Now man
your positions right away!

50
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:36.000
We're going after the Straw Hat pirates.

51
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.570
The Straw Hats?!

52
00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:42.940
Not bad.

53
00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:45.680
So a final farewell,
o' kingdom of the sand.

54
00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:46.970
Luffy, aren't you full yet?

55
00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.690
These Alabasta dishes
are great aren't they, Sanji?

56
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.990
You should make 'em sometime.

57
00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:51.890
Yeah, I liked 'em too,

58
00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.060
so I got some recipes from Terracotta.

59
00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.160
I also got some of their local spices.

60
00:03:57.190 --> 00:03:59.660
Um... What's wrong, Nami?
Are you sick?

61
00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.170
I'll give you a
piece of this if you want,

62
00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.090
but just a small one.

63
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.490
Nami, if you're thinking
about Vivi again,

64
00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.030
I understand.

65
00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.360
Listen. Moping around
about it won't help.

66
00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.500
I know it must be really hard
for you. You two got close.

67
00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.700
Just keep your chin up, 'kay?

68
00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:19.060
It's not that.

69
00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.670
I'm just sad we didn't take the reward.

70
00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:28.000
The one billion Berries.

71
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:29.000
– Gah!
– Gah!

72
00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.870
You're moping about the money?!

73
00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.570
Agh! Usopp fell off!

74
00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.870
You shouldn't mislead
people like that, Nami!

75
00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.610
What did you
think I was upset about?

76
00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:38.610
We just walked away
from a huge payday

77
00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.880
that we actually earned!

78
00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.540
Guys, Usopp fell down!

79
00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:42.910
That's his problem!

80
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:44.740
– But you caused it!
– But you caused it!

81
00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:47.140
Karoo! Wake up!

82
00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.000
You're needed!

83
00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.060
It's no use, Igaram.

84
00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:52.290
But the world
government has released

85
00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.890
new bounties on their heads.

86
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.130
We should at least warn them.

87
00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.130
I had the Duck
Squadron take them.

88
00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.860
Even if Karoo could catch up to them,

89
00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.290
it wouldn't change anything.

90
00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:01.320
Why's that?

91
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:02.560
Those new bounties...

92
00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:04.160
They'll actually make them happy.

93
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.390
They'll all be tickled pink.

94
00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.190
But Princess, they...!

95
00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.830
Trust me, they'll be fine!

96
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:08.930
Now out you go!

97
00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:10.430
I've got to get some rest.

98
00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.500
I've got a big day tomorrow, remember?

99
00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.120
Oh, that's right!

100
00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.090
Your coming-of-age ceremony
is tomorrow morning

101
00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.190
at ten!

102
00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:18.160
Uh-huh.

103
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:20.930
Now come on, Karoo.
Let's get some sleep.

104
00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:29.140
Igaram...

105
00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.910
Something's bothering me.

106
00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:32.110
Hey!

107
00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.080
She's awfully calm.

108
00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.750
Strange. Very strange.

109
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.840
It's really quiet,
isn't it, Karoo?

110
00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:50.440
We haven't had a night this quiet in a long time.

111
00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.010
The cook who guards the refrigerator

112
00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.710
from a late-night
raider is gone.

113
00:05:56.780 --> 00:05:59.680
So too is the swordsman who trains every night.

114
00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:03.880
The navigator who throws
pillows when she's asleep.

115
00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:05.820
Her, too. They're gone.

116
00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.120
Snail communication? From who?

117
00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.920
Don't know.
He called himself Bon.

118
00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.320
Just Bon? That's it?

119
00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:16.520
Uh, never heard of the guy.

120
00:06:16.590 --> 00:06:19.920
That's strange. He insists
that you're all good friends.

121
00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.260
Friends with us?

122
00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:25.370
Hello? Hey,
old friends, it's me!

123
00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.010
I betcha never thought you'd
hear from me again, did...?

124
00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.080
You freak! Shut up!

125
00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.880
So you escaped, Mr. 2,
and what do you want?

126
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:37.650
Straw Hat!

127
00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.980
I'd recognize that voice anywhere!

128
00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.550
You're right, I escaped,

129
00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.890
and I wanna keep it that way,
so don't call me Mr. 2!

130
00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.880
If the Marines intercept
this call, they'll be able

131
00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.800
to ascertain the locations
of both me and you!

132
00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.220
Thanks a lot, you jerk!

133
00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.860
Tell us what you want!

134
00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.530
Oh, it's not what I want.

135
00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.720
It's what I have. Your ship!

136
00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:57.720
– Stop joking!
– Stop joking!

137
00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.320
I'm gonna kick your
butt for saying that!

138
00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.090
Where are you?

139
00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.330
On your ship, the Going Merry!

140
00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:03.830
I shoulda kicked him harder!

141
00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:07.870
Hey! Calm down! Please!

142
00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:11.640
I mean, we are friends, right?
Right.

143
00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:20.680
He's at the upper
part of the Sandora River.

144
00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:21.680
Can we trust him?

145
00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:24.310
We did become friends that one time, but...

146
00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:26.820
That was before we knew
he was part of Baroque Works!

147
00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:28.760
I guess we have no choice.

148
00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.320
You're right. He has our ship.

149
00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.880
If he tries to trick us,

150
00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.380
I'll be more than happy
to kick the crap

151
00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:34.210
out of him again.

152
00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:35.450
All right. We gotta move, guys.

153
00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.620
Hey, you guys...

154
00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.060
I, uh... I don't...

155
00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:47.230
I don't know what to do.

156
00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.670
If you were me, what would you do?

157
00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.170
Vivi, we can give you
twelve hours to make a decision.

158
00:07:54.290 --> 00:08:04.210
<b>Current Location:
Alubarna</b>
<b>Sandora River</b>
<b>Nanohana</b>

159
00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:57.010
We'll travel down the Sandora

160
00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:00.080
after teaching Ballerina Boy
why he shouldn't steal from us

161
00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:04.210
<b>Eastern Port</b>

162
00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.110
and by noon tomorrow,

163
00:08:01.150 --> 00:08:02.980
we'll draw near
the eastern harbor.

164
00:08:03.020 --> 00:08:05.080
I doubt we'll be able to drop anchor, though.

165
00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.650
If you do decide to join us,

166
00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:09.100
that's gonna be the only
chance for you to come aboard.

167
00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.940
Twelve o'clock, on the dot.

168
00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:11.940
It's your choice.

169
00:08:11.940 --> 00:08:15.280
You could stay a princess.
or become a pirate.

170
00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.820
I'm sure being
a pirate doesn't compare

171
00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.420
to being a princess,
but we'd sure love to have you.

172
00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:21.760
Yeah, so why wait?
Come with us now, Vivi!

173
00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.920
Knock it off, Luffy.

174
00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:24.480
– Yeah, come on!
– Why?

175
00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:26.250
Don't you guys want her to join us?

176
00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.320
We do, but that's
something she has to decide

177
00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:29.660
for herself!

178
00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:36.980
Twelve o'clock on the dot.

179
00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.020
If it's the eastern harbor,
it'll take four hours

180
00:08:39.050 --> 00:08:40.420
to get there on Karoo.

181
00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:43.320
If I left here by eight,
I'd make it on time.

182
00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.330
Life as a pirate, huh?

183
00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:47.230
Adventures on the
high seas surrounded

184
00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:49.200
by loyal friends.

185
00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:50.900
If I miss this chance,
I know I'll never get

186
00:08:50.930 --> 00:08:53.200
another one like it
for the rest of my life.

187
00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.430
On the other hand, I have
duties here as a princess.

188
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.250
And at a critical
time since this land's

189
00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.780
in the midst of a rebirth.

190
00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:07.620
Whatever I do choose,

191
00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.490
you'll stay with me, won't you?

192
00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.260
Say... Karoo?

193
00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.900
What would you like to do?

194
00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:20.900
Finally!

195
00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:22.900
Long time no see, my friends!

196
00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.370
Did you guys miss little ole me?

197
00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:26.570
Not a bit.

198
00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:27.350
Let's unload!

199
00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:29.550
Later, ducks,
thanks for the lift!

200
00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.820
Yeah! You ducks
take care of yourselves.

201
00:09:31.850 --> 00:09:32.950
Have a safe trip!

202
00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:34.960
Say bye to the
King, the old tube hair guy,

203
00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.440
and all the others for us!

204
00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.270
So long, fellas!

205
00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.990
Farewell!
May you ugly ducklings...

206
00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.440
...turn into beautiful swans!

207
00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.380
Wait, hold on!

208
00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:48.310
Yeah, what?

209
00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.280
Don't "yeah, what" me!
That's just rude!

210
00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.450
You should learn some manners, pretty boy!

211
00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:52.850
Friends aren't supposed
to talk to their friends

212
00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:53.810
that way!

213
00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:55.120
Quit saying that, you weirdo!

214
00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.590
We're not friends, we're enemies!

215
00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:57.260
You lied to us!

216
00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.160
No, I didn't!

217
00:09:58.190 --> 00:09:59.820
I just didn't mention
that I was a member

218
00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.930
of Baroque Works!

219
00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:03.800
Besides, none of that
really matters now does it?

220
00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.770
Baroque works is done for now,

221
00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.200
and that means that
we're no longer enemies.

222
00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.140
Hey, move it!

223
00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.110
Oh, my bad.

224
00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.440
Well if we're not enemies,
Ballerina Guy,

225
00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.450
then why the heck did you steal our ship?

226
00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:16.150
Oh, how dumb are you?

227
00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.100
Watch it!

228
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.730
Listen, if I hadn't
taken your little ship

229
00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.700
from where it was moored,

230
00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.700
what do you think
would've happened to it?

231
00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.570
The Marines probably would have seized it.

232
00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.470
Change that "probably"
to a "definitely,"

233
00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:27.450
honey!

234
00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.880
The Marines have
been looking all over

235
00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.050
for you guys and your ship!

236
00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:33.220
Every port in the country's
been blockaded. Lockdown.

237
00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:34.170
Hey, hold on.

238
00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.440
Are you telling us you
took the Going Merry

239
00:10:36.470 --> 00:10:37.670
so the Marines wouldn't?

240
00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:39.160
– Really?
– How come?

241
00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.440
'Cause you guys are my friends!

242
00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.720
Oh, gimme a break, guys!

243
00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.090
We may have had to fight on opposite sides of a war,

244
00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.460
but our friendship
will last all of eternity!

245
00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:50.540
Need help loading?

246
00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.340
Nope, this is the last one.

247
00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.610
Friends? Yeah, right.

248
00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:55.080
Tell the truth, Twinkle Toes.

249
00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.550
You and your crew don't have a chance

250
00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:57.940
of getting through
that blockade,

251
00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:00.870
but you might if you
had us as allies, right?

252
00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:01.670
Bon Clay!

253
00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:02.540
That's right, you got me,

254
00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.610
but in trying times
such as these

255
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.180
we have to band together under the flag of friendship!

256
00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.080
If you believe in true
friendship, say "aye"!

257
00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:13.830
– Aye!
– Aye!

258
00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.760
– Aye!
– Aye!

259
00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:18.090
Thanks, Straw Hats!

260
00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:19.960
Where were you guys?

261
00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:20.820
Miss Hina!

262
00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:22.930
We've spotted the
Straw Hats' ship!

263
00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:25.600
It's near the upper reaches
of the Sandora River!

264
00:11:25.630 --> 00:11:27.430
What do you think we should do, Captain?

265
00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:30.740
Attack, of course.

266
00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.300
Igaram! I will!

267
00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:38.000
I will be Queen of the Pirates!

268
00:11:56.420 --> 00:11:58.360
Vivi!

269
00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.120
Oh. Good morning, Igaram.

270
00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.120
What's the matter?
You're sweating.

271
00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.250
Enough!

272
00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.600
Where are your manners?
You can't just barge in here!

273
00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:12.620
The princess needs
her privacy, now, go!

274
00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.490
Please forgive me!

275
00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.390
I, um, just wanted
to say good morning!

276
00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:17.620
Is that all?

277
00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:18.890
Ah, no, I mean yes...

278
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.460
Quit blabbering!
What are you still doing here?

279
00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.290
I told you to get out!

280
00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.950
I guess it was my imagination.

281
00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.380
Huh?

282
00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.410
Oh! Your Majesty!

283
00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:34.280
I didn't see you there.
Good morning.

284
00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:36.450
Yes. Good morning.

285
00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:39.590
You too, huh?
Terracotta can be quite scary.

286
00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:42.190
What did you do,
try to say, "Hello"?!

287
00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:46.160
I don't know, Terracotta...

288
00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.360
Isn't this too tight?

289
00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.490
This is how formal
attire is supposed to fit

290
00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:51.160
upon a princess.

291
00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:54.730
I heard that the Square
is already full of people.

292
00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:55.800
Really?

293
00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.200
When it was announced
that your speech

294
00:12:57.240 --> 00:12:58.590
would begin promptly at 10,

295
00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.990
everyone started
getting anxious.

296
00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.830
No one wants to miss a word.

297
00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.400
Your coming-of-age
ceremony should have been

298
00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.000
held two years ago
when you were 14.

299
00:13:07.030 --> 00:13:08.940
Since it was delayed so long,
it's made the people

300
00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:12.140
even more excited
for this special event.

301
00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.940
But I don't have any
pressing information

302
00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:14.810
to share with them.

303
00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.640
They're coming because they love you.

304
00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:19.310
You don't have to say one word.

305
00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:21.380
All you do is show up
and let everyone see

306
00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.160
how much you've grown.

307
00:13:23.230 --> 00:13:24.660
The coming-of-age
ceremony is held

308
00:13:24.730 --> 00:13:26.730
to celebrate you becoming an adult.

309
00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:28.470
It's not about speeches.

310
00:13:28.500 --> 00:13:30.240
And you should be mindful
of the king's feelings

311
00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.270
in taking the time for it.

312
00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.370
Oh, yeah!

313
00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.410
I heard your speech today
is going to be broadcast

314
00:13:35.420 --> 00:13:37.590
throughout all of Alabasta
with transponder snails

315
00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:40.460
and amplifiers. How exciting!

316
00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:42.630
I'm really looking forward to it.

317
00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.420
I received a report
that a battle broke out

318
00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:46.390
at the harbor.

319
00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:47.560
I see.

320
00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.400
In light of this,
you realize we can no longer

321
00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:50.460
get involved.

322
00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:55.230
Fire! Fire!

323
00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:58.600
Dammit! Shoot cannonballs!

324
00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.560
I can't deflect pointy things!

325
00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.700
Seriously. Gimme a break!

326
00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.140
If we take any more iron spears

327
00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:06.100
to the bottom of the ship,

328
00:14:06.180 --> 00:14:08.920
it'll just be a matter
of time before we sink!

329
00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:11.180
More!

330
00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:18.130
Hey! I can't keep plugging
these holes, you guys!

331
00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.360
Don't just stand there!
Do something!

332
00:14:20.360 --> 00:14:21.290
What more can we do?

333
00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.900
It takes all our effort to protect one side!

334
00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:28.370
One ship versus eight isn't a fair fight!

335
00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:31.970
If this was hand-to-hand combat,
we'd have a better chance!

336
00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.020
We're stuck!

337
00:14:33.050 --> 00:14:34.650
Whether we chase them or run away,

338
00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.220
they won't change
their formation!

339
00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:44.120
The "Black Spear Formation"!

340
00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.360
It's a work of art!

341
00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:49.400
It's the Black Cage
Unit's specialty! Ha!

342
00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.360
Idiots!

343
00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:53.870
Hey! Hypnotist!
I thought you were a pirate!

344
00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:54.900
I am!

345
00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:57.440
Now why don't ya shut up!
My reasons are my own!

346
00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.770
Where do I know that guy from?

347
00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:02.030
It took a long time,
but I finally found'em!

348
00:15:02.030 --> 00:15:03.760
That annoying,
crazy cook and his gang

349
00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:04.930
of violent cutthroats!

350
00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:10.000
Here, today! I vow to sink 'em.

351
00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:11.670
Stare at this ring.

352
00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:13.710
You're about to
help me finally prove

353
00:15:13.710 --> 00:15:16.040
that I'm not a weirdo. In fact,
my services alone

354
00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.950
will pave the way to victory.

355
00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:20.550
Hurry!

356
00:15:20.580 --> 00:15:22.220
One! Two!

357
00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:26.760
Jan!

358
00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.130
Who?

359
00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.350
Brother!

360
00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.460
Whoa...!

361
00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:36.400
Usopp! Did you do that?

362
00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:39.130
Amazing!

363
00:15:39.130 --> 00:15:40.970
Yes! Just as I calculated!
It was me!

364
00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.400
That's what happens to enemy
ships when I'm on the job! Yeah!

365
00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.070
That was amazing, Nosie!

366
00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.860
The ships in the
south have all sunk!

367
00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:50.100
Now nothing can prevent us from breaking through!

368
00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:52.870
Bon Clay! We got trouble!

369
00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:54.420
What's wrong?

370
00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:57.040
– Black Cage!
– No!

371
00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.140
What's going on?

372
00:15:58.210 --> 00:16:00.380
Black Cage Hina!
She's a Marine captain!

373
00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.780
We're in her jurisdiction!

374
00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.280
She's a real pain!

375
00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.110
We need to hurry up
and fly the coop!

376
00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.230
– Yes, sir, Mr. Bon Clay, sir!
– Yes, sir, Mr. Bon Clay, sir!

377
00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.230
Seems we've weakened
them quite a bit.

378
00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:12.930
There's no ship
we can't take down

379
00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.470
using our Black Cage Formation!

380
00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.030
Don't get too confident.

381
00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.640
Underestimating criminals such as these

382
00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.270
can come at the expense of one's own life.

383
00:16:20.300 --> 00:16:21.540
Now remember once we arrive,

384
00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.230
you guys are to stay
back or you might get

385
00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:25.470
in my way and then Hina
would be annoyed.

386
00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:26.330
– Yes, ma'am!
– Yes, ma'am!

387
00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:28.330
You guys need to wake up!

388
00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:29.570
We have to run!

389
00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:31.420
If we can pass through that point in the south,

390
00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:32.860
we can escape!

391
00:16:32.890 --> 00:16:34.930
But if we don't change course immediately,

392
00:16:34.990 --> 00:16:36.580
they'll take us down for sure!

393
00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:37.740
If you wanna go, go.

394
00:16:37.780 --> 00:16:39.410
We can't go that way.

395
00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:41.520
And exactly why not?!

396
00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.350
Mr. Bon Clay,
we need to set sail

397
00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.420
while we still can!
There's no more time, sir!

398
00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.480
Noon at the eastern harbor.

399
00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.210
We've got an appointment.

400
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.720
There's no time to go around.

401
00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.280
We'll go straight through.

402
00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:54.790
What?! Suicide! It's ludicrous!

403
00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:56.520
Is there some treasure
you're not telling me about

404
00:16:56.550 --> 00:16:58.520
that's worth throwing
away your lives?

405
00:16:58.520 --> 00:16:59.760
Fine! Run off and die!

406
00:16:59.840 --> 00:17:01.950
We have to go get
one of our friends.

407
00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:15.400
So, it's for your
pal that you risk it all.

408
00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.480
Vivi, I'm coming in, okay?

409
00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:28.630
Sure, the door's open.

410
00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:30.860
Sweetie, what did
you want to talk...

411
00:17:33.510 --> 00:17:35.650
Vivi, amazing.

412
00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.800
I mistook you
for the queen in her youth.

413
00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.510
Uncanny resemblance
and just as beautiful.

414
00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.540
A vision of elegance.

415
00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:43.810
Have a seat, Daddy.

416
00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:48.550
No. Father. Igaram.

417
00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.970
I have an important matter to discuss.

418
00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.870
Great Bon Clay!

419
00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:00.770
"Bon Kurei"

420
00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.980
Running now would go against everything

421
00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:02.010
Bon Clay stands for.

422
00:18:02.040 --> 00:18:04.450
If we abandon allies
who are risking their lives

423
00:18:04.480 --> 00:18:08.380
to pick up a friend, could we
live with ourselves tomorrow?

424
00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.790
Listen, guys. Straw Hats, too!

425
00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:20.460
What I must say is
of great importance!

426
00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:24.270
Miss Hina!

427
00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:26.200
The enemy ships
are splitting up!

428
00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:27.570
The duck ship is headed south!

429
00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:29.870
The duck is probably
meant as a decoy.

430
00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:32.940
Well... Actually, it appears
the entire Straw Hat crew

431
00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:35.240
is onboard the
duck ship, Captain!

432
00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.510
It's the sheep ship
they're using as the decoy!

433
00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:41.850
Follow the duck!

434
00:18:41.880 --> 00:18:43.550
Return to formation immediately!

435
00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:53.660
Three minutes!

436
00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:57.570
Prepare to attack!

437
00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.570
Ready? Full speed ahead!

438
00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:02.210
So, tell me something.

439
00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:05.610
I am the Straw Hat you idiots are looking for, right?

440
00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:08.450
Or am I?

441
00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:09.400
Miss Hina!

442
00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.230
The sheep ship is heading east!

443
00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:12.100
What?

444
00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:18.910
You must be feeling
pretty stupid right now,

445
00:19:18.940 --> 00:19:20.310
falling for such a simple trick!

446
00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:23.110
See, we're masters of disguise!

447
00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:27.980
As well as friends
to the Straw Hats!

448
00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:37.620
Even if I stray
from my code as a man.

449
00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:41.590
Even if I stray from
my code as a woman.

450
00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:46.060
I could never betray
my basic humanity!

451
00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:49.060
That is the
difference between us!

452
00:19:49.090 --> 00:19:51.160
If my brethren
and I are to fall,

453
00:19:51.220 --> 00:19:52.930
we will fall together,

454
00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:56.560
clinging to our freedom
and watching it bloom!

455
00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:02.970
By... Bon Clay.

456
00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:13.220
Bring it on, sista.

457
00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:16.920
Hina's... humiliated!

458
00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:46.640
Bon Clay!

459
00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.760
I promise you, Bon Clay!

460
00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.660
We will never forget you!

461
00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.440
If we are to fall,
let it be in the sea.

462
00:21:16.500 --> 00:21:20.010
The flower of friendship is rejoicing.

463
00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.740
We don't know
who the ringleader is?

464
00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:26.550
Right. It's an
underground organization.

465
00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:28.580
Even its members know absolutely nothing

466
00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:30.580
about the identity of their boss.

467
00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.150
So, this country's
enemy has no name.

468
00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.220
It's impossible
for us to gather information

469
00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:37.170
on them from the outside.

470
00:21:37.190 --> 00:21:39.960
Further investigation might put the country at risk.

471
00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:42.200
But we do have a lead.
Isn't that correct?

472
00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.930
Yes.

473
00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:48.070
Igaram, do you know
what I'm thinking right now?

474
00:21:48.100 --> 00:21:49.700
No! No, I don't!

475
00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:51.970
Leave me be!
I have to go back to my work!

476
00:21:52.030 --> 00:21:53.130
Igaram!

477
00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:55.700
No! Stop it! This isn't a game!

478
00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:58.910
All the more reason
to be honest with me!

479
00:21:58.940 --> 00:22:01.040
I can't sit around and do nothing!

480
00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:18.960
They're after us again!

481
00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:21.230
Get out of our way!

482
00:22:23.280 --> 00:22:25.110
Look! There she is!

483
00:22:25.150 --> 00:22:26.110
It's Vivi!

484
00:22:26.150 --> 00:22:27.980
Princess Vivi, you're a vision!

485
00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.720
We love you!

486
00:22:31.980 --> 00:22:33.150
Princess!

487
00:22:33.220 --> 00:22:34.620
She's all grown up!

488
00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:35.620
Princess!

489
00:22:44.140 --> 00:22:45.600
Then, Vivi...

490
00:22:45.730 --> 00:22:48.070
Let me ask you
just one question.

491
00:22:49.840 --> 00:22:52.240
It all started on that day.

492
00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:55.200
Are you prepared
to live at all cost?

493
00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:00.040
I went on a little adventure.

494
00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:04.040
Princess Vivi's speech
has started hurry up!

495
00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:05.860
I've been waiting so long!

496
00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:08.150
Oh, it's so exciting!

497
00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:10.850
The ceremony in
Alubarna has finally started!

498
00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:12.630
It was delayed by two hours.

499
00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:13.660
What happened?

500
00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:17.570
Ah, well.

501
00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:19.870
I can only hope it won't cause a commotion.

502
00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:22.310
Come and listen, Koza.
Hey, come on.

503
00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:24.580
Vivi's speech has
already started.

504
00:23:24.610 --> 00:23:26.310
The amplifiers are cranked all the way up.

505
00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.050
I could be underground and still hear every word.

506
00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:31.520
A journey...

507
00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:32.990
...to cross the dark sea.

508
00:23:33.020 --> 00:23:35.560
But, what I found was
a grand adventure.

509
00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:38.560
The sheer vastness of the
ocean was overwhelming.

510
00:23:38.630 --> 00:23:40.630
And yet, it brought me
to a series of islands

511
00:23:40.690 --> 00:23:44.520
so unbelievable
they defied imagination.

512
00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:49.000
With such wondrous environments,
inhabited by strange creatures.

513
00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:51.800
At times, the melody of the waves was quiet,

514
00:23:51.900 --> 00:23:55.000
swaying gently, as if easing my soul.

515
00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:56.770
And there were other times

516
00:23:56.840 --> 00:23:59.270
when the melody was
violently laughing at me,

517
00:23:59.310 --> 00:24:02.220
as if threatening to rip my very heart in two.

518
00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:07.620
In that dark, dark storm.

519
00:24:07.650 --> 00:24:10.960
I encountered a single, small ship.

520
00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:14.480
The ship spoke to me, while pushing me onward.

521
00:24:14.510 --> 00:24:17.180
It said with a clear, singular voice,

522
00:24:17.210 --> 00:24:19.520
"Can't you see the light?"

523
00:24:19.540 --> 00:24:22.610
This wondrous ship,
which never strayed off course,

524
00:24:22.650 --> 00:24:25.020
even through
pitch-black darkness,

525
00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:28.540
danced its way across
the huge waves.

526
00:24:28.590 --> 00:24:31.990
The mighty ship kept its stem pointed straight ahead,

527
00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:35.830
thwarting every obstacle
the ocean could throw at it.

528
00:24:35.860 --> 00:24:39.600
Finally, as the ship roused
my spirits, it said,

529
00:24:39.740 --> 00:24:42.200
"Look! There is a light!"

530
00:24:42.200 --> 00:24:44.700
History will one day
catalog this experience

531
00:24:44.740 --> 00:24:45.840
as an illusion.

532
00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:50.080
But, I will always remember
it as a singular truth.

533
00:24:50.110 --> 00:24:52.080
What's she talking about?

534
00:24:52.110 --> 00:24:55.580
The secret battle she fought
against that group of criminals.

535
00:24:55.620 --> 00:24:57.080
And...

536
00:25:00.600 --> 00:25:01.940
Vivi.

537
00:25:01.970 --> 00:25:04.070
Forget about it.
You heard the speech.

538
00:25:04.110 --> 00:25:06.180
That was Vivi's voice
without a doubt.

539
00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:07.940
They're just broadcasting the ceremony

540
00:25:07.980 --> 00:25:10.010
that's being held in Alubarna.

541
00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:12.700
Vivi's already made up her mind not to come here.

542
00:25:12.700 --> 00:25:16.570
No. I don't buy it.
I say she's here.

543
00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:20.210
<b>Eastern Port
Tamarisk</b>

544
00:25:16.600 --> 00:25:18.800
This is the Tamarisk place, right?

545
00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:20.800
Yeah. That's it.

546
00:25:20.860 --> 00:25:22.590
Let's go. It's past noon.

547
00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:24.110
There's no way
she wouldn't have come!

548
00:25:24.210 --> 00:25:25.880
She's definitely here!

549
00:25:25.950 --> 00:25:26.950
Let's get out and look for her!

550
00:25:26.980 --> 00:25:30.020
This is bad, guys!
The Marines are after us again!

551
00:25:30.030 --> 00:25:32.140
Exactly how many
ships are out there?

552
00:25:32.170 --> 00:25:33.640
I see at least six.

553
00:25:33.670 --> 00:25:35.870
Dammit. Let's move.

554
00:25:35.940 --> 00:25:37.270
Give it up, Luffy.

555
00:25:37.270 --> 00:25:40.210
Vivi's course is on a road far different from ours.

556
00:25:47.510 --> 00:25:49.480
What the hell is going on?

557
00:25:49.440 --> 00:25:53.360
<b>Alubarna</b>

558
00:25:50.650 --> 00:25:51.810
Hey, show your face!

559
00:25:51.810 --> 00:25:53.550
We know you're a fake!

560
00:25:53.580 --> 00:25:55.520
It's Squad Captain Igaram!

561
00:25:55.550 --> 00:25:57.650
Where's the real Vivi?

562
00:25:57.650 --> 00:25:58.690
We heard her voice!

563
00:25:58.720 --> 00:26:01.190
So, where the hell is the
princess speaking from?

564
00:26:05.730 --> 00:26:07.400
At least Vivi is safe.

565
00:26:09.100 --> 00:26:10.240
Everyone!

566
00:26:22.920 --> 00:26:24.620
Vivi!

567
00:26:24.650 --> 00:26:25.520
Karoo!

568
00:26:28.090 --> 00:26:28.990
Vivi!

569
00:26:29.020 --> 00:26:31.360
– See? She came!
– Vivi!

570
00:26:31.360 --> 00:26:33.690
We need to go back!
Better hurry!

571
00:26:33.790 --> 00:26:35.360
The Marines are
right behind us, too!

572
00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:43.100
I came to say goodbye!

573
00:26:45.940 --> 00:26:46.840
What'd she say?

574
00:26:46.870 --> 00:26:48.210
Karoo, handset.

575
00:26:50.970 --> 00:26:54.310
Sorry. But I can't go with you!

576
00:26:54.340 --> 00:26:56.380
Thank you so much
for everything!

577
00:26:58.180 --> 00:27:00.150
Who's the princess talking to?

578
00:27:00.150 --> 00:27:03.180
No way! I think I just
spotted Princess Vivi!

579
00:27:03.220 --> 00:27:06.020
She's supposed to be at the ceremony in Alubarna.

580
00:27:06.060 --> 00:27:08.760
I'd like to go on
more adventures.

581
00:27:08.820 --> 00:27:11.330
But I can't ignore
the needs of my country,

582
00:27:11.370 --> 00:27:13.210
which I love more than anything!

583
00:27:13.240 --> 00:27:15.010
Where is Vivi?

584
00:27:15.010 --> 00:27:16.780
We want our princess,
not a captain

585
00:27:16.780 --> 00:27:17.880
in disguise!

586
00:27:17.880 --> 00:27:18.980
Hey, Princess!

587
00:27:19.070 --> 00:27:20.240
Ya need a shave!

588
00:27:20.240 --> 00:27:21.670
Ma-ma-ma!

589
00:27:21.740 --> 00:27:23.740
Nice dancing, Igaram!

590
00:27:23.800 --> 00:27:25.300
Yeah. Keep it up!

591
00:27:25.300 --> 00:27:27.870
Ha, everyone can
tell those aren't real!

592
00:27:29.200 --> 00:27:30.840
I have to stay!

593
00:27:30.870 --> 00:27:33.310
I hope you understand!

594
00:27:33.340 --> 00:27:34.810
I see!

595
00:27:34.820 --> 00:27:35.920
Thank you.

596
00:27:37.710 --> 00:27:39.680
Our sign needs to be an X.

597
00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:40.420
How come?

598
00:27:40.420 --> 00:27:41.520
We're pirates!

599
00:27:41.520 --> 00:27:43.320
You know that it's
literal translation means

600
00:27:43.350 --> 00:27:45.120
death to one's opponents, right?

601
00:27:45.150 --> 00:27:46.050
That's fine!

602
00:27:46.120 --> 00:27:49.130
It must be an X! It looks cool!
Huh, Vivi?

603
00:27:49.150 --> 00:27:50.720
Yeah, I like it!

604
00:27:50.750 --> 00:27:52.250
It doesn't matter what it is.

605
00:27:52.250 --> 00:27:54.690
That's not the point!
Just write it.

606
00:27:58.180 --> 00:27:59.180
I will...

607
00:28:05.090 --> 00:28:05.920
I...!

608
00:28:05.920 --> 00:28:07.260
This will do!

609
00:28:07.990 --> 00:28:11.130
I will remain here
and fulfill my duty!

610
00:28:13.030 --> 00:28:15.000
It's a sign of our friendship!

611
00:28:16.230 --> 00:28:17.970
If we ever meet again...

612
00:28:19.370 --> 00:28:21.090
No matter how much time's passed,

613
00:28:21.090 --> 00:28:22.960
will you still call me "friend"?

614
00:28:30.370 --> 00:28:31.500
Did you hear that?

615
00:28:31.530 --> 00:28:34.170
The princess has some kinda
bond with the Straw Hats!

616
00:28:34.200 --> 00:28:35.140
Yeah.

617
00:28:35.170 --> 00:28:37.040
Princess Vivi considers those pirates friends?

618
00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:39.420
– You'll forever be...
– Idiot!

619
00:28:39.480 --> 00:28:41.280
Don't reply, got it?!

620
00:28:41.310 --> 00:28:44.310
The Marines now know about Vivi and us.

621
00:28:44.340 --> 00:28:46.280
If they can prove she
has a connection to us,

622
00:28:46.280 --> 00:28:47.480
it's all over.

623
00:28:47.510 --> 00:28:50.380
She'll be considered a criminal.

624
00:28:50.450 --> 00:28:52.280
Turn away. Not another word.

625
00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:35.870
No matter what happens
on that island, remember.

626
00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:37.770
This thing on all our arms

627
00:29:37.840 --> 00:29:39.770
is a sign of our friendship!

628
00:30:21.080 --> 00:30:22.780
Set sail!
